# Cryptography rules: shekyl-core's part

Estate rule [`30-cryptography`](30-cryptography.mdc) holds in every Shekyl repository.
This rule holds the part of it that only shekyl-core has: the protocol's
per-output PQC keys, where its vectors live, and its domain registry.

## Per-output PQC keys (Option C)

PQC signing uses per-output KEM-derived keys, not the wallet master key.
Per-output keys give forward secrecy per output. The ML-KEM ciphertext lives
in `tx_extra` under tag `0x06` and must survive pruning permanently — it is
required for wallet PQC key rederivation.

## Test vectors

shekyl-core's vectors are in `docs/test_vectors/*.json`. A change to one
requires a CHANGELOG entry as well as review: vectors define consensus.

## Domain registry

A live domain string is registered, and its bytes are held by the domain
registry gate: see SIGNATURE_ALIGNMENT §5.
